sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Client Browser UI
    participant WsApi as API Gateway WebSocket
    participant Lambda as Backend Lambda
    participant DynamoDb as DynamoDB Connections

    Note over Client, DynamoDb: 1. Connection Establishment Lifecycle ($connect)
    Client->>WsApi: Connect (GET wss://.../prod)
    WsApi->>Lambda: Synchronous Proxy ($connect)
    Lambda->>DynamoDb: Store Connection (Put connectionId & State)
    DynamoDb-->>Lambda: Put Success
    Lambda-->>WsApi: Return HTTP 200 OK
    WsApi-->>Client: 101 Switching Protocols (Connection Established)

    Note over Client, DynamoDb: 2. Bidirectional Messaging & Push Stream
    Client->>WsApi: Send Message Action (action: "subscribe" / "chat")
    WsApi->>Lambda: Forward Payload ($default route)
    Lambda->>Lambda: Process Message (or Query Bedrock AgentCore)
    Lambda->>WsApi: Push Response Payload (PostToConnection API)
    WsApi-->>Client: Receive Real-Time Stream (WebSocket Message)

    Note over Client, DynamoDb: 3. Connection Termination Lifecycle ($disconnect)
    Client->>WsApi: Close Connection (or network timeout)
    WsApi->>Lambda: Synchronous Proxy ($disconnect)
    Lambda->>DynamoDb: Delete Connection (Delete connectionId)
    DynamoDb-->>Lambda: Delete Success
    Lambda-->>WsApi: Return HTTP 200 OK
    WsApi-->>Client: Connection Closed
